WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.690
<b>Math Prep Room</b>

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:02.690
Good morning!

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.760
Wow!

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.120
My family in the countryside sent them to me.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.110
They got them from a local farmer.

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:13.760
So I'm giving some to everyone!

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:14.490
Lucky us!

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.200
Here, you too, Inuzuka-sensei!

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.120
Is it okay for me to take so much?

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:20.750
Go ahead, go ahead.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:21.580
Um...

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:24.580
They're great just stir-fried 
with salt and pepper!

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.460
Eat a lot, okay?

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:28.920
Yeah...

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.540
I'm back!

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.970
Package for you.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:44.670
What is it? What is it?

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.990
It looks like it's from Grandma.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:53.450
Lots of stuff!

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:54.030
<b>To Kouhei</b>

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.770
A letter from Granny?

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:02.160
"Be sure... to give...

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:07.370
lots of... to...

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.740
Tsumugi-chan."

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:11.760
These are for me?

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.540
Wh-What should we do with 
this mountain of vegetables?

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:50.520
<b>Hated Vegetables and Bits in Gratin</b>

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:53.610
<b>30,000 quick recipes! 
No cooking skills required!</b>

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:53.610
<b>Keyword Search</b>

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:53.610
<b>Vegetable Side Dishes</b>

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:53.610
<b>Search</b>

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.640
Cut, fry...

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:57.400
We can make vegetable stir-fry.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:02.140
But it'll need something else 
before Tsumugi will eat it...

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:08.700
There's no meat...

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:10.660
Meat!

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:16.050
I've got those Hamburg steak 
patties I made for lunch.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.570
I'll write a letter to Granny!

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.290
Meat! I wanna eat meat!

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.540
<b>Granny</b>

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:31.880
Meat! I love meat!

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:34.010
Meat! Meat!

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:40.900
It's done!

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:44.230
Tsumugi, dinnertime!

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:45.660
Okay!

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.250
Food! Foody food!

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:51.370
Daddy did a good job today!

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:58.850
It's all right!

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:00.340
Look, it's Hamburg steak.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:01.940
Come on, it's dinnertime.

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:03.860
Let's eat!

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:06.050
Let's... eat.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:13.890
I think it's okay.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.940
It might even be good!

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:17.650
What do you think, Tsumugi?

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:21.610
Huh?

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:26.490
Try eating the vegetable with the meat.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:29.330
I don't think you'll taste 
the green pepper that much.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.580
I think it came out pretty good...

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:12.760
You tried hard and ate a bite.

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:14.600
Just eat what you can, okay?

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:26.380
Kouhei, you can't eat pork cutlets?

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:29.610
Then I'll trade you.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.090
Here, green peppers.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:37.230
Mom, Nii-chan took Kouhei's meat!

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:39.400
We traded, right, Kouhei?

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.270
Come on, Onii-chan...

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:41.950
It's fine.

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:03.710
Kids' tongues are sensitive,

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:08.720
so they judge anything bitter or sour 
as potentially dangerous, I've heard.

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:11.310
So even if a young child can't eat them,

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:14.780
sometimes they can when they grow up.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:18.400
I've heard that before.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.970
I hated green peppers when I was a kid, too.

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:24.010
You don't look like a picky eater, though.

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:27.070
I kind of was, when I was little.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:29.800
There were vegetables I didn't like.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.410
But my mom

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:34.910
was really strict.

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:37.150
It's okay.

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:39.260
I know you can eat them.

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:40.840
You can do it!

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:45.000
She said it was rude to the food, and the 
person who made it, to not eat it all.

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:49.080
Now I can eat anything, thanks to her.

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:49.970
I see.

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.820
What do you want to do, Sensei?

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:58.100
It's a shame to waste vegetables.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.110
Yes.

00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:01.770
But I don't want to force her to eat them.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.880
Why do people have to eat 
vegetables they don't like?

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:09.480
Because they're good for you,

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:12.610
or because it's better not to be a picky eater?

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:15.240
Those are both true, but...

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:17.760
You can get through life 
without eating green peppers.

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:18.780
That's true.

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:22.930
Am I spoiling her as a parent?

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:26.770
Well, each family has its 
own way of thinking, right?

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:27.590
Yes.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:34.090
Why did I want Tsumugi to eat green peppers?

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:37.020
I wasn't thinking about 
whether it was good for her,

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:40.580
or whether it was better 
to not be a picky eater.

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:45.080
Maybe I wanted her to 
enjoy the happiness I felt

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:48.340
when I ate something delicious.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:54.330
Then let's make something delicious 
with them that she can eat!

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:55.960
C-Can we do that?

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:56.810
Probably!

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:58.740
I'll talk to my mom about it.

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:03.250
Even if she can't eat it, instead 
of just setting it on the table,

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:09.250
she might be more interested if she saw
how much you enjoyed eating it.

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:13.880
Well, see you later.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:14.540
Right.

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:15.970
Let's come up with a schedule.

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:20.790
By the way, what vegetables 
does Tsumugi-chan like?

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:24.150
She loves cherry tomatoes.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:25.900
Cherry tomatoes?

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:29.900
What vegetable didn't you like?

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:31.000
Wasabi!

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:34.460
That's a condiment, isn't it?

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:43.870
<b>Potatoes 
Carrots 
Zucchini 
Squash
Green Peppers
Onions 
Asparagus</b>

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:43.870
<b>Cherry Tomatoes</b>

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:50.740
Make vegetables taste good...

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:54.620
Is Iida-san talking to herself?

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:57.960
If it's bothering you, ask her to eat with us.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:00.730
Go talk to her.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:02.930
But...

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:06.950
She's always eating something during breaks.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:06.190
<b>First Period Break</b>

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:07.350
<b>Second Period Break</b>

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:09.930
If she has no problem eating alone like that,

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:12.440
maybe it's some kind of thing for her?

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:14.780
Kotori!

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:16.650
You make any friends?

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:17.200
Not yet.

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:20.200
You're taking too long!

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:23.910
Even if you're fine without them, 
at least make a few.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:26.170
You're in the next class over, right?

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:27.480
What are you doing here?

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:29.880
I came to check up on you.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:33.370
Sorry I haven't been able to hang out much.

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:35.800
I've been busy helping at the family store.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:39.210
You have to look after your siblings, 
too, so it must be rough.

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:40.140
I guess.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.480
What about you?

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:42.760
Me?

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:46.780
Megumi-san hasn't come to buy 
vegetables that often lately,

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:49.850
so Mom's worried about your restaurant.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:58.120
Hey, do you know any recipes that you can 
use to get kids to eat lots of vegetables?

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:00.620
Why do you ask that?

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:04.230
Well... You know, reasons...

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:09.710
Vegetables kids don't like?

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:11.150
Let me see...

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:14.590
I chop them up into little pieces 
and mix them with foods they like.

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:17.640
Really? But isn't that a lot of work?

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:20.800
I just make my boy eat them, 
whether he likes it or not!

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:24.280
Mommy, I'm not eating 
any more tomatoes, ever!

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:28.020
Hey, Mikio! Your shoes!

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:31.280
Mikio-kun doesn't like tomatoes?

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:32.980
Even though they're so good, huh?

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:36.190
I guess every family does it differently.

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:39.450
Tsumugi, dinnertime!

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:45.220
Okay, now...

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:46.700
Let's eat!

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:03.820
Mom's Recipes

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:06.470
So for today, I'd like to make a gratin.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:08.720
G-Gratin?

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:10.700
We're eating gratin?!

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:11.810
We sure are!

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:15.600
Gratin! Gratin! Gra-gra-gratin!

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:14.040
Why are we making a gratin?

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:18.810
The plan is to cut the 
vegetables into tiny bits,

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:22.560
and hide them in a bechamel sauce, 
which everyone loves!

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:23.450
I see.

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:26.570
If we cut them all into about 
the same size and mix them in,

00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:31.210
there'll be lots of different colors and 
tastes, so it should be a lot of fun!

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:34.960
Won't she realize there are green peppers in it?

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:38.540
Gra-gratin! Gra-gra-gratin!

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:37.510
Tsumugi's smarter than you'd think.

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:39.740
Let's make it fun!

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:42.890
I've heard that when you're 
excited or feeling good,

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:45.320
you can eat things you wouldn't 
normally be able to.

00:11:45.320 --> 00:11:45.970
You've heard?

00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:48.120
I actually got this idea

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:50.930
from someone who knows all about vegetables.

00:11:53.110 --> 00:11:57.500
Tsumugi, I'm going to wash the vegetables.

00:11:57.500 --> 00:11:59.120
Will you help me?

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:00.150
Okay!

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:03.610
It's cold!

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:07.580
Does it feel good?

00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:09.320
Yup!

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:11.510
ROFL, daddy!

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:14.790
Did you learn that in kindergarten?

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:16.040
Next is...

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:18.590
What's this red thing?

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:21.870
A red bell pepper.

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:22.380
Pep...

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:25.550
It's okay!

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.530
It's only in the same family 
as green bell peppers.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:29.340
Look.

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:33.810
When you cut it in half 
and take out the seeds,

00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:36.440
it's red all the way inside!

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:43.700
It looks more like a cup than a pepper.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:46.450
Sensei, can I have a word?

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:52.260
Here you go.

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.050
I can have it?

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:07.640
More!

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:09.760
We'll be eating soon, so just a little, okay?

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:11.290
Okay!

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:16.160
It's sweet!

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:17.950
Daddy, have some, too.

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:19.230
Ahh...

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:21.750
Yeah, it's sweet.

00:13:29.960 --> 00:13:32.870
Okay, now that the veggies are clean,

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:35.260
cut them into bite-sized chunks...

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:37.260
The squash is so hard.

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:40.000
To cut hard squash easily...

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:42.250
You can use this, it says.

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:44.090
A cooking chopstick?

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:46.380
Just one?

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:46.760
Yes.

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:50.840
You stick it into the center of the squash,

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:53.830
and poke it all the way in.

00:13:56.240 --> 00:14:00.860
Take out the chopstick and stick 
the knife in the hole from above.

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:01.980
From above?

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:02.820
From above.

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:05.030
Like you're stabbing it into the hole.

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:07.990
It went in easily!

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:18.240
Then we cut the other 
vegetables into bite-sized bits.

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:18.950
Okay!

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:24.590
Like this?

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:28.490
Let's make them a little smaller.

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:29.340
Roger.

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:32.710
Parboil the carrots and fava beans.

00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:37.500
Put olive oil in the frying pan,

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:41.620
then fry the chicken thigh 
you've cut into bite-size pieces.

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:46.740
Fry the harder vegetables first.

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:49.580
Should we take the chicken out first?

00:14:49.580 --> 00:14:50.860
Oh, right.

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:53.670
Squash.

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:56.370
Zucchini.

00:15:00.740 --> 00:15:02.110
Potatoes in!

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:03.340
In!

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:06.680
Lastly...

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:27.240
Then the chicken,

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:31.050
and the parboiled veggies go in.

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:33.400
We'll bake it in the oven to finish up,

00:15:33.400 --> 00:15:36.740
so you don't need to be super careful 
about making sure it's cooked.

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:38.700
I'll put a little salt in, too.

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:40.120
And then...

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:44.670
We put this in an oven-safe pan.

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:48.380
Oh, no! We have to flatten out the veggies!

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:51.240
Tsumugi, will you help?

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:52.800
Okay!

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:53.690
Spatula!

00:15:53.690 --> 00:15:54.800
Here!

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:01.040
Well?

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:02.700
Splendid!

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:04.080
A genius!

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:06.070
She's cute, and she's a genius!

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:10.610
Now the fillings are all set.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:12.990
It's time to make the sauce!

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:15.020
A white sauce?

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:16.560
A bechamel sauce.

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:17.770
A becha...

00:16:17.770 --> 00:16:18.790
Bechamel.

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:21.710
How are they different?

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:23.260
Um...

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:28.290
Like, there's the white sauce family, 
and the bechamel sauce genus?

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:33.600
All white-colored sauces used in European
cooking are called white sauces,

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:38.800
but the bechamel sauce is a particular one
 made with a milk base and a roux...

00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:39.840
A roux?

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:41.060
We're about to make that now.

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:48.720
Take the sliced onions and 
fry them in plenty of butter,

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:50.440
being careful not to burn them.

00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:52.740
Slowly, on low heat.

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:54.950
Once they're soft,

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:58.040
add the weak flour, and then stir.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:16:58.940
Okay!

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:04.040
Huh?

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:05.420
It looks kinda dry.

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:07.460
Did I mess up?

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:10.170
I-It's okay.

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:12.430
Lets keep at it until there are no more clumps.

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:13.210
Okay.

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:15.380
Tsumugi.

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:19.390
Can you cast a spell so there 
won't be any clumps?

00:17:19.910 --> 00:17:21.010
Okay!

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:24.240
Clump, clump...

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:26.350
No clumping!

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:27.980
No clumping!

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:29.070
It's starting to come together... maybe?

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:30.760
No clumps... Clump, clump!

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:31.230
Then let's put the milk in.

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:34.500
Add just a little at a time 
so that it doesn't clump up.

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:35.240
Clump, clump... No clumps...

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:37.770
No clumping!

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:39.340
Then mix with a whisk.

00:17:38.460 --> 00:17:40.620
Clump, clump...

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:43.910
Tomorrow will come!

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:44.150
Then dissolve a boullion cube in it.

00:17:44.150 --> 00:17:46.210
No clumps!

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:48.890
How's it look?

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:51.530
It's clumped!

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:53.370
Sensei!

00:17:55.060 --> 00:17:56.470
This is an onion!

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:58.120
Oh, it is.

00:17:58.120 --> 00:17:59.430
Thank goodness!

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:03.720
It's looking really good!

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:06.120
The clumps are gone, and it's pretty now!

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:09.440
Yeah! Looks like your magic spell worked!

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:10.890
Really?

00:18:10.890 --> 00:18:12.440
Clump! Clump!

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:14.900
Thank you, Tsumugi!

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:19.260
Now we pour this on...

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:23.510
Tsumugi-chan.

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:24.950
What?

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:28.370
Will you put these on top of the gratin?

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:31.210
Cherry tomatoes!

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:33.950
You went out and got some for us?

00:18:33.950 --> 00:18:34.670
Yes.

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:37.880
The goal for today is to 
make vegetables yummy.

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:40.640
You like cherry tomatoes, 
don't you, Tsumugi-chan?

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:41.680
I do!

00:18:46.550 --> 00:18:48.640
You too, Kotori-chan!

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:49.420
Okay.

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:55.930
Put on the cheese.

00:18:58.210 --> 00:18:59.320
Okay!

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:05.210
Cook for fifteen minutes in
a 250-degree Celsius oven.

00:19:08.720 --> 00:19:10.430
Now we can take a break.

00:19:10.430 --> 00:19:11.780
Good work.

00:19:26.510 --> 00:19:28.460
It's ready!

00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:30.730
Tsumugi-chan, it looks good, huh?

00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:31.920
Yeah!

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:35.260
I washed the veggies and flattened them,

00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:37.390
and put on the tomatoes, 
and put on the cheese!

00:19:37.390 --> 00:19:38.640
Wow!

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:40.560
You worked hard, huh?

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:41.240
Yup!

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:42.990
Now we'll dish it up.

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:49.790
I can eat four cherry tomatoes!

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:50.460
Okay!

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:55.980
Let's eat!

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:10.730
It's good!

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:12.030
Sensei!

00:20:12.030 --> 00:20:14.690
Yes, this is better than I'd hoped!

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:17.320
What is this?!

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:19.950
This goo!

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:21.820
It's sauce. A white sauce.

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:23.260
A bechamel sauce.

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:25.290
A bechamel sauce.

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:27.080
Becha-sauce!

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:31.040
This is wonderful!

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:32.880
The vegetables inside are...

00:20:32.880 --> 00:20:35.640
Um... They're just good!

00:20:35.640 --> 00:20:38.220
Daddy, this is a tomato!

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:41.030
You squish it and eat it, and it's good!

00:20:42.310 --> 00:20:45.690
This green thing is good, too.

00:20:45.690 --> 00:20:47.390
It's asparagus.

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:48.750
Aspas!

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:51.370
It's friends with the red thing.

00:20:58.340 --> 00:21:00.440
I ate something bitter.

00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:02.970
You ate the bell pepper?

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:05.240
Yeah. It was bitter.

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:06.820
I'll eat something sweet.

00:21:07.220 --> 00:21:08.720
I see.

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:11.290
You swallowed it, even though 
it was bitter. Good for you!

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:14.500
Good for me!

00:21:17.160 --> 00:21:18.960
Here we go, here we go...

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:21.920
Here, Daddy!

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:23.490
Open wide!

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:25.850
Can I?

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:27.230
Open wide!

00:21:27.230 --> 00:21:28.820
Ahh!

00:21:32.950 --> 00:21:35.000
What's wrong, Sensei?

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:37.770
Under the cheese...

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:40.680
were all of her bell peppers.

00:21:43.730 --> 00:21:45.580
The becha sauce is yummy!

00:21:47.190 --> 00:21:49.240
Well, let's take our time.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:53.850
She can get used to it little by little, 
and we'll hope for the best in the future.

00:21:54.550 --> 00:21:55.960
You sound like a teacher.

00:21:57.360 --> 00:21:59.960
Thank you for the food!
